Preserve the Panther Lake sensor power policy while adopting native CVS.

Omarchy's existing intel-ipu7-camera package clears rgbcamera_pwrup_host
for the Panther Lake USBIO power path. Scope the equivalent native policy
to the INTC10E1 Synaptics controller; retain other platforms and privacy
ownership. This carries the existing policy forward, pending hardware
validation with the native driver's runtime PM and V4L2 integration.

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/cvs/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/cvs/core.c
@@ -95,6 +95,12 @@
 		if (cvs_quirk_table[i].vid == vid &&
 		    cvs_quirk_table[i].pid == pid) {
 			ctx->quirks = cvs_quirk_table[i].quirks;
+			/* PTL Synaptics firmware sequences the sensor power. */
+			if (vid == 0x06cb && pid == 0x0701 &&
+			    has_acpi_companion(cvs_dev(ctx)) &&
+			    acpi_dev_hid_match(ACPI_COMPANION(cvs_dev(ctx)),
+					       "INTC10E1"))
+				ctx->quirks &= ~ICVS_HOST_SENSOR_PWR_CTRL;
 			dev_info(cvs_dev(ctx),
 				 "Quirks: 0x%lx (VID:0x%04x PID:0x%04x)\n",
 				 ctx->quirks, vid, pid);
